rlm-tfplan [TERRAFORM-PLAN-ARGS...]

Run `terraform plan -out latest.tfplan` in the current directory, so
the plan can be reviewed and then applied unchanged. On success it
prints the exact `terraform apply <plan-file>` command to run next.

Refuses to run when `terraform` is not on `$PATH`, or when the current
directory contains no `*.tf` / `*.tf.json` files — that check turns the
common "wrong directory" mistake into an immediate error instead of a
confusing terraform message about an empty configuration.

Any extra arguments are passed straight through to `terraform plan`,
so flags like `-target=`, `-var-file=`, `-refresh=false` and
`-destroy` work as usual. The function's own exit status is
terraform's.

This is the function form of the older `tp` alias, which remains
available.

ARGUMENTS
  TERRAFORM-PLAN-ARGS   Optional; forwarded verbatim to
                        `terraform plan`.

ENVIRONMENT
  TFPLAN_FILE   Plan output filename (optional, default
                `latest.tfplan`). Note that the `ta` alias always
                applies `latest.tfplan`, so a custom name must be
                applied with the printed command instead.

REQUIRES
  terraform
